Source
------
nand2mario/ddr3-tang-primer-20k @ a6d866d2369eb27e99cedee6c0cb8a09f311fa57
(2023-07-25). That tree's controller is the later of the two upstream
copies. NESTang's last Primer 20K controller is 8b8f4fa6 (2022-10-30,
deleted from NESTang in 0e0a1e1 when Nano 20K landed). It matches
a6d866d except it latches dout on data_ready and uses RCALIB_COUNT=16.
NESTang does not subtract a fixed write-level backoff.

Local deltas
------------
- RCALIB_COUNT is 16 on silicon, matching the NESTang Dock controller.
  dout stays the live dq_in[0] word from a6d866d. The bridge samples it
  on the data_ready pulse, which is the latch's data_ready value too.
- Each byte lane write-levels on its own DQ. Upstream uses one wstep
  for both lanes.
- A read pulses WLOADN high for one pclk at the end of READ. Upstream
  ties WLOADN low. HOLD stops the write clock (UG286 / prim_sim
  fclk_hold). The falling edge reloads WSTEP before the next store.
- The bridge waits 16 controller clocks after busy falls, including
  after a refresh, before the next command.
- dm_out's default is nonblocking, so the write unmask reaches OSER8_MEM
  on this pclk. Serializer inputs are cleared while reset is held.
- `ifdef SIM shortcuts are labeled in the controller. They are not the
  silicon path. Icarus gets an explicit genvar.
- After the read gate, training writes eight halfwords (every DQ bit,
  the neighbour column, and both bytes) and requires the whole word
  back in dq_in[0]. The scan is offsets -4..+12 from each lane's own
  write-level edge. Offsets -4..-1 are the cliff. Silicon finishes
  that lane-0 row. Three matches at the edge or above lock that
  center. Stopping at the first three matches locks the cliff when
  it false-passes (Dock steps 0007/0009) and a later store comes
  back with its high byte replaced. A row that matches only on the
  cliff still locks the cliff. The Micron model passes only below
  its write-level edge, and a write on that edge slips the sim
  strobe, so the sim path keeps the first three matches (steps
  22/23). `+eye_decide` is the silicon choice on that model: a cliff
  at indices 0..2 and a window at 5..7 lock center 6 (steps 22/28).
  The first such row locks that lane-0 step and the lane-1 center.
  No pass leaves read_calib_done low, so the LED stays dark.
  dq_in[0] is sampled on the pclk after data_ready rises, which is
  the beat the CPU sees while data_ready is high.
- Icarus does not finish the vendor 255-tap DQS cascade.
  sim/patch_prim_dqs.py copies prim_sim and replaces that cascade
  with constant transport delays (N*0.025 ns, 1 ps early). The
  vendor file is not modified. A variable delay sits on a CK edge
  and the Micron model drops the strobe.

